Scale Up
========

Overview
--------
This builds on the secured and monitored infrastructure by scaling up
to 4 servers total: 2 load balancers (configured as a cluster), and
2 servers where each component (web server, application server, and
database) is now split onto its own dedicated server.

Components added and why
-------------------------
- 1 additional load balancer (HAProxy), clustered with the existing
  one: removes the load balancer as a SPOF. If one load balancer
  fails, the other can take over, since they are configured together
  as a cluster (e.g. active-active or active-passive) sharing a
  virtual IP.
- 1 additional server, and splitting the web server, application
  server, and database onto their own dedicated servers: each
  component now has dedicated CPU, memory, and disk resources, so a
  spike in one component (e.g. the database) no longer impacts the
  performance of the others (e.g. the web/app server). It also allows
  each layer to be scaled independently based on its own needs.

Summary of why each element is added
--------------------------------------
- 2nd load balancer: eliminates the load balancer SPOF and allows
  continuous availability of the entry point to the infrastructure.
- Dedicated web server machine: can be scaled/tuned purely for
  handling HTTP requests and static content.
- Dedicated application server machine: can be scaled/tuned purely
  for running the business logic, independent of web server load.
- Dedicated database machine: can be scaled/tuned purely for data
  storage and retrieval performance, isolated from the web/app layer
  load.
